historic-routing (@VERSION@) unstable; urgency=low

  * Development build (NOT released): native Debian packaging for Debian 13
    amd64, built from source commit @COMMIT@ (FRR base @FRR_COMMIT@).
  * Package split: historic-routing-runtime (libfrr.so.0, zebra, vtysh,
    configuration skeleton) and historic-routing-egp (egpd + its unit).
  * Both packages are bound to one build: exact version dependency plus the
    historic-routing-abi marker @ABI@ (source commit + FRR base commit).
  * Installed under @PREFIX@; the distribution FRR (/etc/frr, /usr/sbin/frr*,
    frr.service, libfrr in /usr/lib) is not modified.
  * Sockets and PID files live in @RUNSTATEDIR@ (systemd RuntimeDirectory),
    not in the install prefix.
  * Services are installed but neither enabled nor started.
  * RUNPATH of the shipped binaries is $ORIGIN/../lib, so libfrr is loaded only
    from this project's own prefix.

 -- Chenlang Li <Cc1580155hsg@163.com>  @DATE@
